  "content": {
    "id": "p5-p1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "Show that the following expression has the same value for every nonzero value of $n$.\n\n$$\\frac{1}{n}+\\frac{(n+1)(n-1)}{n}-(n+1)$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$-1$ for every $n\\ne0$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{n}+\\frac{(n+1)(n-1)}{n}-(n+1)&=\\frac{1+n^2-1}{n}-(n+1)\\\\&=\\frac{n^2}{n}-(n+1)\\\\&=n-(n+1)\\\\&=-1\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe value is constant for all $n\\ne0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 25
  },
